--   Uniqueness of a prime above its contraction to a cyclic fixed field
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields, let $\sigma\in\operatorname{Aut}_K(L)$, and put $E=L^{\langle\sigma\rangle}$. Let $Q$ be a prime ideal of $\mathcal O_L$ with $\sigma(Q)=Q$. For every prime ideal $Q'$ of $\mathcal O_L$,
--
--   $$
--   Q'\cap\mathcal O_E=Q\cap\mathcal O_E\quad\Longrightarrow\quad Q'=Q.
--   $$
--
--   The extension $L/K$ need not be Galois, and no unramifiedness assumption is required.
--
--   This excludes splitting above the contraction to the cyclic fixed field while permitting ramification.
